From 20eb8a45995ed0eb7892103dfcdbdc01d6887ff8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 09:28:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hir_typeck: a trait object unsizes to one that adds an auto
 trait implied by its data trait

qh3 2.0.4 (py314-qh3) src/hpke.rs:49-50

    pub struct HpkeContext { sealer: Box<dyn HpkeSealer + Send>, .. }
    ..
    let (enc, sealer) = match suite.setup_sealer(info.as_bytes(), &pk) { .. };
    Ok(Self { sealer, enc })

with rustls 0.23.45's `fn setup_sealer(..) -> Result<(EncapsulatedSecret,
Box<dyn HpkeSealer + 'static>), Error>` and `pub trait HpkeSealer: Debug +
Send + Sync + 'static` failed with `error:0: Type mismatch between dyn
(HpkeSealer+Send) and dyn (HpkeSealer+'#omitted) - trait counts differ`.

rustc's unsize coercion between trait objects may add auto traits that are
supertraits of the data trait (1.90 rustc_trait_selection
candidate_assembly.rs: "We may upcast to auto traits that are either
explicitly listed in the object type's bounds, or implied by the principal
trait ref's supertraits").  mrustc's three dyn->dyn unsize checks
(expr_cs.cpp check_unsize_tys, helpers.cpp's TraitObject arm and
static.cpp can_unsize, which MIR lowering also uses for pointer casts)
required every destination marker to be listed on the source, so the
coercion fell back to an equality and the types mismatched.  MIR cleanup
already treats a same-data-trait unsize as a plain fat-pointer copy.

HIR_TraitObject_ImpliesMarker (static.cpp) accepts a marker listed on the
source or an auto trait among the data trait's flattened parent traits
(so `Derived: Base: Send` works too); the three sites use it.  A trait
without the supertrait is still rejected.

Assisted-By: Claude Fable 5.1
